    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>In the bounds of darkness hiding from light...</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>In the soul of every nightmare...</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>In the deepest ravines that lay beneath our world...</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>In the chasmic rifts of time...</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dragged into a dark conspiracy, explore and survive your way through the beginning of the end for the nation of Australia. Use your wits and instinct to stay alive in this 2000s-style FPS horror adventure set Down Under during the 1990s.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Explore</strong> the city streets of suburban Australia, enormous abandoned mansions and ancient cities that lay beneath the bottom of the ocean</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Utilise multiple weapons</strong> from <strong>magnum revolvers</strong> to <strong>double barrel shotguns</strong> to survive</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Face a variety of <strong>horrifying creatures</strong> ranging from <strong>spiders the size of small cars</strong> to <strong>walking fish monsters</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fully immersive environment</strong> allows for <strong>complete interaction</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Photosourced visuals</strong> on the <strong>Source Engine</strong> for the <strong>authentic early 2000s game experience</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Build your own campaigns</strong> using the included Amygdala: Prelude\u00a0 Source SDK</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A terror awaits in a cycle that challenges the very fabric of society, beneath which it lays dormant. It sleeps down in the dark, waiting for the day that it shall rise up and return to power.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>True horror cannot die. It only waits for the right moment of return.</strong></p>",
